3. TECH STACK (use exactly this)
Frontend: React 18 + Vite (JavaScript/JSX, not TypeScript), React Router v6, Tailwind CSS v3, framer-motion (animations), lucide-react (icons), fuse.js (fuzzy matching), tesseract.js v5 (browser OCR), html5-qrcode (barcode), date-fns (dates), react-hot-toast (toasts).
Backend: Node.js 20 + Express, better-sqlite3 (database, file medlens.db), cors, dotenv, node-fetch (or built-in fetch), zod (request validation).
AI: Anthropic Messages API via plain fetch (POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages), key from env ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, model from env LLM_MODEL (default claude-sonnet-5-5). Optional: if the key is missing, use the deterministic fallback.
Free external data: openFDA, RxNorm/RxNav, DailyMed (no keys required).
Dev setup for Replit:
One project with /client and /server folders and a root package.json.
Root script "dev": "concurrently \"npm --prefix server run dev\" \"npm --prefix client run dev\"".
Vite dev server on host: 0.0.0.0, port 5000, with server.proxy forwarding /api to http://localhost:3001. Set allowedHosts: true in the Vite config for Replit preview.
Express on port 3001.
Configure the Replit run command as npm run dev.
No authentication, no Firebase, no Docker.
