6.7 Parsing and matching logic (server POST /api/identify, body { ocrText, barcode? })
Expiry regex candidates: (EXP(?:IRY)?\.?\s*(?:DATE)?\s*[:\-]?\s*)(\d{1,2}[\/\-\.]\d{2,4}|[A-Z]{3,9}\.?\s*\d{2,4}|\d{4}[\/\-]\d{2}). Normalize to the last day of the month. Reject dates earlier than 2000 or later than 2100. If a MFG date is also present, make sure EXP > MFG. If not, flag as unclear.
Batch: (B\.?\s*No\.?|Batch(?:\s*No\.?)?)\s*[:\-]?\s*([A-Z0-9\-]{3,}).
Strength: (\d+(?:\.\d+)?)\s*(mg|mcg|g|ml|iu|units).
Name match: Fuse.js over brand_names, generic_name, ingredients[].name (threshold 0.4). Then boost or penalize using strength and ingredient agreement: if the strength found in the text matches a record’s strength → +confidence; if the brand matches but the strength conflicts → flag “Packaging information does not match the database record”.
Confidence: High ≥ 0.8, Medium 0.5–0.8, Low < 0.5. Return the top 3 candidates so the UI can show “Is this your medicine?” chips when confidence isn’t High.
Barcode: look up medicines.barcode. If found, confidence is High. If not, return an empty result with a manual-search prompt.
Response shape: { extracted: {name, strength, ingredients[], form, manufacturer, expiry, batch}, candidates: [{medicine, score}], best, confidence, checks: [{key, status:'ok'|'warn', message}] }.
